  "name": "Example: Integrating Secant-Tangent and Cosecant-Cotangent",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int (-\\csc x\\cot x)\\,\\textrm d x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\csc x \\cot x \\, \\textrm dx = - \\csc x + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (-csc\u2061xcot\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int (csc\u2061xcot\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(-csc\u2061x)+C \\\\  & =csc\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
